What are the Linux Directory Commands?

pwd – The command displays the present working directory or
        your current directory path.ex->$ pwd
ls – This command lists the contents of a directory.ex->$ ls <options> <directory>
cd – This lets you switch from one directory to another.ex-> $ cd/home/downloads
mkdir – The command creates a new empty directory.ex->mkdir newdir
rmdir – The command deletes or removes an empty directory.ex-> $ rmdir wrk/
failed to remove as directory is not empty
rm – Removes one or multiple files. Used with -R option to remove a
    non-empty directory.ex->rm -rf wrk/

What’s the command to check the disk space usage on a Linux system?
use $ df command
Typing df -h will display the disk space in a human-readable format,
showing the used and available space for all mounted file systems.\

How to List All Processes Running on a Linux?
 $ ps aux

How To view hidden files
 $ ls -a

Why is the tar command used?
The tar command is used for extracting or creating an archived file.
If you wish to extract all of the files from the sample.tar.gz package,
use the following command:
$ tar -xvzf sample.tar.gz

How do you move a file from one directory to another using Linux commands?
Moving a file from one directory to another is performed using the mv command
in Linux. $ mv <oldname> <newname>
If you want to move a file named “example.txt” from the current directory to
 another directory called “folder”, you would type mv example.txt folder/.
$ mv example.txt folder/

copy command
$ cp <oldname> <newname>

What Linux command could you use to display the list of users currently
logged into the system?
Displaying the list of users currently logged into the system can
be done with the who command.
 $ who

How do you change the permissions of a file in Linux?
$ chmod
You can change a file’s permissions in Linux using the chmod command.
This command is used to set different access rights like read, write, and
execute for the file owner, group, and others.
For example, if you want to add execute permission to the owner,
you can use chmod u+x filename.

What command could you use to display the contents of a text file
in the Linux terminal?
The contents of a text file in the Linux terminal can be displayed
by using the cat command followed by the file name. For example,
cat file.txt will show the content of “file.txt”.
$ cat file.txt

What are the Different Types of Permissions in Linux?

Read (r) – Allows users to read files or list a directory.
Write (w) – Allows the user to modify or edit files.
Execute (x) – Allows users to run the file.

owner->rwx
group->rw_
other->r_x

What is the Grep Command?
Grep is a command line tool for searching and matching text files or
lines in a text file.
$ grep [options] pattern [files]

The following command counts the number of occurrences of the string
‘Unix‘ in file1.txt.
$ grep -c "unix" file1.txt

What’s the difference between the grep and awk commands?
The awk command allows you to define actions based on patterns and
perform arithmetic operations on text.
The grep command focuses on searching and displaying lines matching specific criteria.

How to Terminate a Running Process in Linux?
To terminate or kill a process, use the kill command followed by the
PID of the process.
$ kill PID

To terminate an unresponsive process/forcefully, pass the -9 option shown
$ kill -9 PID

To kill a process by name, use the killall command followed by the process name.
For example, to terminate the Firefox process, run the command:
$ killall firefox

Check How Long the Linux System Has Been Running?
$ uptime

How to Check Linux System Information?
To check basic system information such as kernel name and version, hostname,
and operating system
$ uname -a